7. Compositor: reel/showcase/v2/index.html plus v2/film.js, run in headless Chromium and deterministic. A pure pose(t) returns:
- the camera (framing solver, keyed moves, three cuts, drift, lean with 2400 px perspective, phone at z +18);
- the take frame each device shows (with holds);
- the cursor and touch marks from the meta logs;
- the URL pill text, and the status-bar fill and glyph colour;
- the overlays (screen-space DOM in General Sans and Cabinet Grotesk loaded from app/fonts) and the two chips.
Device frames and shadows are SVG or DOM. Screens come from take frames pre-scaled with Lanczos3 (sharp), in two mip levels. The Linen stage gets the Paper falloff. Each output frame averages three sub-frames at t−8.333, t and t+8.333 ms with weights 1:2:1, then adds σ 1.2/255 dither.
